 @AdamSibbs  I've broken down my power consumption of my PC currently which is running a 65w Ryzen 5 7600 with an 1060 6gb card that runs on 120w and that alone costs me £1.50 per day to run. The 4070 has an extra 43% power consumption compared to my current setup and so this will cost me £2.14 per day while the 7800xt has a 77% power consumption increase and this will cost me £2.60 per day.

I'm currently unemployed and my PC is my life and so while my math is for heavy use daily, I did do the math if I was working and it would average 8 hours per day (accounting for the weekend days off) and even then it would cost me about £100 more per year to run.

I can tell you the average daily costs of my PC because I spent a whole month using just my PC, 2 LED lights and 30 minutes to cook per day lol I'd check my meter every 3 hours to get the costs of everything I used so my averages are solid.

